cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use MetriPlane, please cite the software release."
title: "MetriPlane v0.2.0: Open-Source Physical Observability for Workcell Evidence, Replay, and Regression Testing"
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: "Parkkinen"
    given-names: "Miko"
version: "0.2.0"
date-released: "2026-06-17"
license: "MIT"
repository-code: "https://github.com/Miko997/metriplane"
url: "https://github.com/Miko997/metriplane"
abstract: >-
  MetriPlane v0.2.0 is open-source physical observability software for workcell
  evidence, replay, and regression testing. It maps tagged/fiducial assets into
  calibrated planar XY state, evaluates spatial contracts, emits incidents,
  builds replayable evidence bundles, generates physical regression tests and
  Cell Truth Reports, and exposes read-only operator review workflows. The
  release preserves the historical v0.1.3/v0.1.4 evidence lineage while serving
  as the main SoftwareX paper artifact.
keywords:
  - research software
  - digital twins
  - robotics
  - industrial automation
  - physical observability
  - deterministic replay
  - zone analytics
  - ArUco
  - planar homography
  - reproducibility
